Source attribution and scope

reactingFoamPAD derives from OpenCFD OpenFOAM-v2012 reactingFoam and the pre-existing local timed solver. Original OpenFOAM copyright/license headers are retained. The numerical equations are unchanged; project timing code is added.

costEulerImplicit copies the per-cell StandardChemistryModel integration loop from OpenFOAM v2012, retaining its numerical order, and derives from the existing EulerImplicit solver. This derivative is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later. OpenFOAM Foundation/OpenCFD copyright remains applicable.

The public counterFlowFlame2DLTS case is copied from the installed OpenCFD v2012 tutorial into retained benchmark directories. It is not original geometry or an independently validated chemistry mechanism.

Scotch is used through the existing OpenFOAM decomposition plugin; no graph-partitioner source is newly authored. Python plotting dependencies are build-time packages in ignored build/pydeps and retain their own licenses. Literature sources are cited, not redistributed as full papers.

All new source/documentation/analysis in this project is GPL-3.0-or-later. See LICENSE.
